---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import PosterBand from "../components/PosterBand.astro";
import ResearchNav from "../components/ResearchNav.astro";
import Timeline from "../components/Timeline.astro";
import CloseStrip from "../components/CloseStrip.astro";
import matrix from "../data/progress.json";

type Cell = { text: string; kind: string };
const cells = matrix.cells as Record<string, Record<string, Cell>>;
---

<Base path="/progress/">
  <PosterBand path="/progress/">
    <Fragment slot="title">A promise needs<br /><em>a record.</em></Fragment>
    <p slot="intro">
      We want Arkansas’s investment decisions to change. Here is how we distinguish a public commitment from instructions,
      repayments, and an end to new purchases.
    </p>
    <ResearchNav path="/progress/" />
  </PosterBand>

  <div class="wrap progress">
    <section class="margin-grid part" aria-labelledby="start-title">
      <h2 id="start-title">The starting point</h2>
      <div class="prose">
        <p>
          The records currently available show historical investments and funding. They do not establish an official
          commitment to stop new purchases or a withdrawal resulting from the campaign.
        </p>
        <p class="provenance">
          Last reviewed: September 28, 2026. We update this page when new documents establish a change. This date identifies
          our review, not necessarily when an agency provided records.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="margin-grid part" aria-labelledby="new-title">
      <h2 id="new-title">New purchases on the record</h2>
      <div class="prose">
        <p>
          Records received in September 2026 show Arkansas institutions adding to Israel Bonds, not stopping. A preliminary
          custody report APERS produced for September 7, 2026 lists a second Israel Bond, $10 million, for $25 million on that
          report. ATRS’s manager bought a $9.9 million Israel Bond in February 2026, and its second-quarter report sets a
          long-term objective of more Israel Bonds, no more than $10 million a year.
        </p>
        <p>
          <a href="/investments/#apers">See the APERS records</a>. <a href="/investments/#atrs">See the ATRS records</a>.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="margin-grid part" aria-labelledby="check-title">
      <h2 id="check-title">What we will check</h2>
      <div class="prose">
        <ol class="checks">
          <li><strong>Commitment:</strong> an attributable written statement identifies the institution, scope and timetable.</li>
          <li>
            <strong>Implementation:</strong> a board resolution, policy change, or investment instruction puts the commitment into
            effect.
          </li>
          <li><strong>Receipt:</strong> records show principal was actually received, with the amount and date.</li>
          <li>
            <strong>Continued exclusion:</strong> subsequent holdings and transaction records show whether new purchases, renewals
            or reinvestments occurred.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Campaign contribution:</strong> correspondence or another attributable record supports a connection to the
            campaign. An ordinary maturity alone does not establish that connection.
          </li>
        </ol>
        <p>A new purchase after a commitment, a rejected demand, or a failure to implement belongs in this record when documented.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="wide matrix">
        <h3 class="matrix__title" id="pm-title">Where each institution stands</h3>
        <p class="matrix__scope">Status on each check at our September 28, 2026 review, using the definitions above.</p>
        <div class="table-region reflow">
          <table role="table" aria-labelledby="pm-title">
            <thead role="rowgroup">
              <tr role="row">
                <th scope="col" role="columnheader">Check</th>
                {matrix.institutions.map((i) => <th scope="col" role="columnheader">{i}</th>)}
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody role="rowgroup">
              {
                matrix.checks.map((check) => (
                  <tr role="row">
                    <th scope="row" role="rowheader">{check}</th>
                    {matrix.institutions.map((inst) => (
                      <td role="cell" data-label={inst}>
                        <span class:list={["status", `status--${cells[check][inst].kind}`]}>{cells[check][inst].text}</span>
                      </td>
                    ))}
                  </tr>
                ))
              }
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
        <p class="matrix__note">
          “Second bond added” and “bought” come from the new purchases section above. “No maturity yet” means no bond in that
          record has reached its maturity date.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="margin-grid part" aria-labelledby="next-title">
      <h2 id="next-title">October and November: check the next decision</h2>
      <div class="prose">
        <p>
          The June 2025 Treasury statement scheduled two $5 million positions to mature on October 1, 2026 and one $10 million
          position on November 1, 2026. We will compare those entries with a later inventory, actual receipts, and subsequent
          investment activity before reporting a change.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="wide">
        <Timeline id="mt-progress" />
        <p class="after">
          <a href="/investments/#treasury">See the positions and their source</a>. <a href="/take-action/#officials"
            >Ask the Treasury for a written commitment now</a
          >.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>

  <CloseStrip />
</Base>

<style>
  .progress {
    padding-block: var(--s-6) var(--s-8);
  }
  .part {
    padding-top: var(--s-8);
  }
  .part .prose {
    margin-top: var(--s-4);
  }
  .checks li {
    padding-left: 0.2em;
  }
  .wide {
    max-width: 62rem;
  }
  @media (min-width: 60rem) {
    .margin-grid > .wide {
      grid-column: 1 / -1;
    }
  }
  .matrix {
    margin-top: var(--s-7);
  }
  .matrix__title {
    font-size: var(--step-2);
  }
  .matrix__scope,
  .matrix__note {
    margin-top: var(--s-3);
    font-size: var(--step--1);
    color: var(--olive-ink);
    max-width: 44em;
  }
  .matrix th[scope="row"] {
    font-weight: 700;
  }
  /* Statuses print as words; weight and ink, not badges. */
  .status--no {
    color: var(--olive-ink);
  }
  .status--na {
    color: var(--olive-ink);
    font-style: normal;
    text-decoration: underline dotted;
    text-underline-offset: 0.2em;
  }
  .status--against {
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--ink);
  }
  .after {
    margin-top: var(--s-5);
  }
</style>
